WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.227 --> 00:00:02.787
- Interns,

00:00:02.787 --> 00:00:05.720
it's not what you're going 
to learn this summer.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.375
As a matter of fact,
94% of you are gonna

00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:09.101
take jobs where
they're gonna teach

00:00:09.101 --> 00:00:10.552
you dumbass shit

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:12.248
or stuff that you already know.

00:00:12.248 --> 00:00:14.188
They're mailing in 
their internships.

00:00:14.188 --> 00:00:17.954
Interns, it's not about what
you're going to learn

00:00:17.954 --> 00:00:19.109
this summer, my friends,

00:00:19.109 --> 00:00:20.846
it's going to be who you meet.

00:00:20.846 --> 00:00:23.743
Please understand as you 
go into this internship

00:00:23.743 --> 00:00:26.156
maximize networking.

00:00:26.156 --> 00:00:27.577
Shake hands,
kiss babies.

00:00:27.577 --> 00:00:29.107
If you're a wallflower,

00:00:29.107 --> 00:00:30.885
don't even do internships.

00:00:31.695 --> 00:00:33.215
Not the classic way.

00:00:33.215 --> 00:00:34.760
Obviously, you have 
a skill to learn.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.303
You're lucky enough 
to be a developer

00:00:36.303 --> 00:00:38.263
or something like that but fine.

00:00:38.263 --> 00:00:40.233
But if you're an intern,

00:00:40.233 --> 00:00:43.123
please understand it is
the human connections

00:00:43.123 --> 00:00:44.126
that you're gonna make.

00:00:44.126 --> 00:00:45.965
Way too many people
roll in and think they're going

00:00:45.965 --> 00:00:47.921
to learn something 
about advertising or

00:00:47.921 --> 00:00:50.725
marketing or media or startups.

00:00:50.725 --> 00:00:52.426
You're not.
You're just not.

00:00:53.706 --> 00:00:55.602
You're not.
Just saving you time.

00:00:55.602 --> 00:00:57.833
And if you do,
it's just this much.

00:00:57.833 --> 00:00:59.798
It's 3% of the equation.

00:00:59.798 --> 00:01:01.603
Please attack the other 97.

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:03.592
Go to every after hours event.

00:01:03.592 --> 00:01:05.716
Say hello to everybody.

00:01:05.716 --> 00:01:07.747
If you go into an office where 
everybody's head down,

00:01:07.747 --> 00:01:09.302
it's not that kind of culture,

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.324
figure it out.
Hack it.

00:01:11.324 --> 00:01:13.588
Be the obnoxious intern 
that was too bubbly.

00:01:13.588 --> 00:01:16.989
And make sure you 
attach yourself,

00:01:16.989 --> 00:01:18.657
even if you go into 
an office, law firm

00:01:18.657 --> 00:01:20.269
where everybody is head down,

00:01:20.269 --> 00:01:21.947
if you see that 
one person that looks up

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:24.099
and gives you a 
glimmer of people skills

00:01:24.099 --> 00:01:25.738
attach yourself to that person.

00:01:25.738 --> 00:01:27.058
Let them bring you to things.

00:01:27.058 --> 00:01:30.821
Interns, use this time wisely.

00:01:30.821 --> 00:01:33.655
Way too many of you
go in and you think

00:01:33.655 --> 00:01:34.941
you're gonna get something.

00:01:34.941 --> 00:01:37.751
And in reality, the magic
was sitting right in front of you.

00:01:37.751 --> 00:01:39.813
And the punchline, my friends,

00:01:39.813 --> 00:01:41.347
is it's the people.

00:01:41.347 --> 00:01:42.510
It's the people.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.475
It's the people that you meet
in that office that go work

00:01:44.475 --> 00:01:47.149
somewhere else, that are
reminded by your hustle

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:49.368
and tenacity and good natureness

00:01:49.368 --> 00:01:53.648
and offense and you went for it,
you attached for it

00:01:53.648 --> 00:01:55.232
you wanted it

00:01:55.232 --> 00:01:56.362
and they're the ones that

00:01:56.362 --> 00:01:57.745
give you the opportunities.

00:01:57.745 --> 00:01:59.149
This is a very simple world.

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:00.829
This is a people world.

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:02.921
Not the black and white 
skills you learned this

00:02:02.921 --> 00:02:05.176
summer in eight weeks.

00:02:05.176 --> 00:02:07.334
Half of you are going to get 
coffee and do dumb shit

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:10.348
'cause they disrespected 
you inappropriately.

00:02:11.238 --> 00:02:13.544
So please, even if you 
are in that 50% that's getting

00:02:13.544 --> 00:02:15.890
dumb shit and coffees and
things of that nature,

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:18.828
say hello. Drop a coffee off
to somebody and they've

00:02:18.828 --> 00:02:20.717
got a Cardinals pennant
and you know something

00:02:20.717 --> 00:02:22.591
about the Cardinals,
say something.

00:02:22.591 --> 00:02:25.230
Say something about
Adam Wainwright.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.312
Create relationships.

00:02:27.312 --> 00:02:28.897
It is the only KPI.

00:02:28.897 --> 00:02:33.249
It is the only ROI of
an internship.

